What Exactly Are Basic String Operations?

Standard Definition:

A String operation is an action you can perform on a string (a piece of text) in Java. These operations help you manipulate text, like finding the length of a string, comparing two strings, combining strings, or extracting part of a string.


1. Java String split() — what it does
-- split() breaks one string into multiple parts using a separator (delimiter) and returns a String array.
-- trim() removes extra spaces from the beginning and end of a string.
-- What substring() does
-- It is used to extract a part of a string.
-- parseInt() converts a String into an int value.


Creating a String
String s1 = "Hello";
String s2 = new String("Hello");
2. String Length
String s = "Java";
int len = s.length();
3. Convert to Uppercase and Lowercase
s.toUpperCase();
s.toLowerCase();
4. Character at Specific Index
char ch = s.charAt(2);
5. Compare Strings
s1.equals(s2);
s1.equalsIgnoreCase(s2);
s1.compareTo(s2);
6. Concatenation
String s3 = s1 + s2;
String s4 = s1.concat(s2);
7. Substring
s.substring(1);
s.substring(1, 4);
8. Contains
s.contains("va");
9. StartsWith and EndsWith
s.startsWith("Ja");
s.endsWith("va");
10. Index Of
s.indexOf('a');
s.lastIndexOf('a');
11. Replace
s.replace('a', 'o');
s.replace("Ja", "Ta");
12. Trim (Remove Spaces)
String s = "  Java  ";
s.trim();
13. Convert Number to String and String to Number
int num = 10;
String str = String.valueOf(num);

int n = Integer.parseInt("123");
14. Convert to Char Array
char[] arr = s.toCharArray();
15. Split
String s = "Java Python C";
String[] words = s.split(" ");
